abstract: >-
  A research-prototype biological content classifier built using Anthropic's
  Constitutional Classifiers methodology. It defines a 56-rule biosafety
  constitution across 7 NSABB categories, generates synthetic and reuse-only
  training data, and fine-tunes DeBERTa-v3-base classifiers, culminating in a
  dual-mode guard (a v8bh response head plus an experimental prompt head). The
  project's durable contribution is its evaluation discipline: leakage-clean
  splits, size-peer benchmarking, per-source contamination control, and five
  documented self-audits that each reversed a prior conclusion. The honest
  result is a negative one: the response head sits in the recall band of 7-9B
  guards but is Pareto-dominated by the openly-available Qwen3Guard-0.6B and is
  not bio-selective (selectivity S=1.03). Released as a research artifact and
  methodology case study, not a production safeguard.
